        <!-- FAQ -->
        <section id="faq" class="ed-faq scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>Frequently asked questions</h2>
          <details open>
            <summary><h3>Does Wayfair sell good treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Wayfair sells mostly walking pads and budget folding treadmills from direct-to-consumer brands, plus some house-label listings. Some are reasonable buys. Judge each listing on whether it names a manufacturer you can identify, whether its specifications describe a treadmill and agree with other sources, and whether the warranty and return terms are clear. Established fitness brands were not prominent when we checked.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Who makes Wayfair house-brand treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Wayfair does not make them. It says it has over one hundred house brands and sources from about 20 thousand suppliers, and independent reporting describes house-brand items as supplier products sold under Wayfair names. The listing usually does not name the maker, so ask Wayfair in writing for the manufacturer and model number before buying a house-label treadmill.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>What is the Wayfair return policy on treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Wayfair accepts returns on most items within 30 days of delivery, for a refund or store credit, and refunds can take up to 14 business days. Independent guides say return shipping is usually deducted from the refund unless the item is damaged or defective, items should be in original condition and packaging, and non-returnable listings are excluded. Check the listing first.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Is a Wayfair protection plan worth it on a treadmill?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Sometimes. Plans are provided by Allstate and administered by SquareTrade, can be added up to 90 days after purchase, and for mechanical products generally start after the manufacturer's warranty ends. It can make sense on a daily-use machine with a short base warranty. Read the terms for exclusions and how fitness equipment is categorised before buying.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Wayfair deliver and assemble treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Wayfair arranges delivery, by parcel carrier for small items and by freight and last-mile agents for large ones, and many listings offer paid professional assembly. What delivery includes varies by listing, from a parcel left at the door to room-of-choice service. Check the delivery type and whether assembly affects returns before ordering.
            </p>
          </details>
          <details>
            <summary><h3>Does Wayfair price match treadmills?</h3></summary>
            <p class="faq-a">
              Do not count on it. Wayfair's help centre has a price-matching article, and independent guides say Wayfair does not match competitors' prices, though it may consider a drop in its own price shortly after purchase. Because Wayfair prices change frequently, compare the same model on other sites before you buy rather than after.
            </p>
          </details>
        </section>

        <!-- Why trust us -->
        <section id="why-trust-us" class="ed-trust not-prose">
          <h2>Why trust Treadmill Reviews USA?</h2>
          <p>
            Every recommendation is checked against the numbers that matter for a treadmill: the maker's own
            listing and manual, at least one independent source, the warranty terms and the CPSC recall
            database. Where sources disagree we say so rather than pick a number, we say plainly when a
            machine has not been tested hands-on, and we never accept payment for a placement. <a href="/editorial-standards/">Read our review process.</a>
          </p>
